{"id":14,"text":"One day, the wind and the sun argued. “I am stronger than you,” said the wind.\n\n“No, I am stronger,” said the sun.\n\nThey saw a man walking down the road. He wore a thick coat.\n\n“Let’s have a test,” said the sun. “Whoever can take off his coat is the strongest.”\n\n“Easy!” said the wind. He blew very hard. Whoosh! The man held his coat tightly. The wind blew harder, but the man held it even tighter.\n\nThe wind got tired. “I give up,” he said. “Now it’s your turn.”\n\nThe sun came out slowly. It shone warm and bright. The man felt warm and smiled. Soon he felt very hot. He took off his coat and sat in the shade.\n\nThe wind was surprised. “How did you do that?”\n\nThe sun said, “I was gentle and kind. Being strong is not always the best way.”\n\nMoral: Kindness works better than force.","tr":null,"gl":{"one":"bir, bitta","day":"kun","the":"(aniq artikl)","wind":"shamol","and":"va","sun":"quyosh","argued":"bahslashdi","i":"men","am":"-man (to be)","stronger":"kuchliroq","than":"-dan (ko'ra)","you":"sen, siz","said":"dedi","no":"yo'q; hech qanday","they":"ular","saw":"ko'rdi","a":"bir (noaniq artikl)","man":"odam, kishi","walking":"yurib","down":"pastga","road":"yo'l","he":"u (erkak)","wore":"kiydi","thick":"qalin","coat":"palto","let":"ruxsat bermoq; qani, ...aylik","have":"ega bo'lmoq; bor","test":"sinov","whoever":"kim bo'lsa ham","can":"qila olmoq","take":"olmoq","off":"(dan) tushib, uzoqlashib","his":"uning","is":"-dir (to be)","strongest":"eng kuchli","easy":"oson","blew":"esdi; pufladi","very":"juda","hard":"qattiq; qiyin","whoosh":"vush (ovoz)","held":"ushladi","tightly":"mahkam","harder":"qattiqroq, qiyinroq","but":"lekin, ammo","it":"u (narsa)","even":"hatto","tighter":"mahkamroq","got":"oldi, bo'ldi","tired":"charchagan","give":"bermoq","up":"yuqoriga","now":"hozir, endi","your":"sening, sizning","turn":"navbat; burilmoq","came":"keldi","out":"tashqariga","slowly":"sekin-asta","shone":"porladi","warm":"iliq","bright":"yorqin","felt":"h